---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---
<BaseLayout
  title="Privacy Policy"
  description="Privacy policy for the personal Home Assistant integration connecting Google Nest devices to a private, self-hosted instance."
>
  <section class="section">
    <div class="container privacy-container">
      <h1>Privacy Policy</h1>

      <div class="policy">
        <p class="lede">
          This page covers the personal Home Assistant integration used to connect Google Nest
          devices (thermostat, doorbell, camera) to a private, self-hosted Home Assistant
          instance for personal home automation.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>What data is accessed:</strong> Device state and status (e.g. temperature,
          on/off, motion/doorbell events) from Nest devices authorized via the Google Smart
          Device Management API.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>How data is used:</strong> Solely to display and control these devices within
          a private Home Assistant instance running on personal hardware, for personal
          household use.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Data sharing:</strong> Data is not sold, shared, or transmitted to any third
          party. It is not used for advertising, analytics, or any purpose beyond personal home
          automation.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Data storage:</strong> Device state data is processed locally on personal
          infrastructure. No data is stored on behalf of external users, as this integration
          serves a single household.
        </p>

        <p>
          <strong>Contact:</strong> Questions about this integration can be directed to
          <a href="mailto:matt.coalson@gmail.com">matt.coalson@gmail.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .privacy-container { max-width: 680px; }
  h1 { margin-bottom: var(--space-l); }
  .policy p {
    font-size: 1.05rem;
    line-height: 1.8;
    margin-bottom: 1.5em;
  }
  .policy .lede {
    padding-bottom: 1.5em;
    border-bottom: 1px solid var(--color-rule);
  }
  .policy strong { font-weight: 500; }
</style>
